## FINAL SUMMARY

- **BEST**: Candidate 4 — 0.0400 ms
- Schedule: forall tile_sizes [8,0] (16 threads) + tile_for [0,0,64] (K outer) + tile_for [4,8,16] (register) + vectorize [4,8,16] + unroll K_inner ×4
- Vectors: vector<4x8x16xf64> = 512 elements (at limit)
- Speedup vs baseline (6.307ms): **157.8x**
- Speedup vs PyTorch (0.0355ms): **0.888x (1.13x slower)**

### Best Transform Schedule
```
module attributes {transform.with_named_sequence} {
  transform.named_sequence @__transform_main(%arg0: !transform.any_op) {
    %matmul = transform.structured.match attributes{tag = "operation_0"} in %arg0 : (!transform.any_op) -> !transform.any_op
    %tiled_forall, %forall_op = transform.structured.tile_using_forall %matmul tile_sizes [8, 0]
      : (!transform.any_op) -> (!transform.any_op, !transform.any_op)
    %tiled_k, %kloop = transform.structured.tile_using_for %tiled_forall tile_sizes [0, 0, 64]
      : (!transform.any_op) -> (!transform.any_op, !transform.any_op)
    %tiled_reg, %mloop, %nloop, %kloop_inner = transform.structured.tile_using_for %tiled_k tile_sizes [4, 8, 16]
      : (!transform.any_op) -> (!transform.any_op, !transform.any_op, !transform.any_op, !transform.any_op)
    transform.structured.vectorize %tiled_reg vector_sizes [4, 8, 16] : !transform.any_op
    transform.loop.unroll %kloop_inner {factor = 4} : !transform.any_op
    transform.yield
  }
}
```

### Key Learnings (vs previous run on same shape)
- [4,8,16] + unroll×4 beats [4,8,4] + hoist: 0.040 vs 0.051 ms (22% improvement)
- Larger K inner (16) with full unroll produces more compute per FMA group
- 16 threads (M-only) is optimal for M=128 (8 rows per thread)
- K outer=64 is optimal; K=32 too many iterations, K=128 spills L2
- Unroll is better than hoist for this shape with [4,8,16] vectors
- 2D parallelism [8,4] worse — N-partitioning fragments B matrix
